WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Agent Readiness Gate — production evidence for an AI agent: software you install in your own cloud, on every release.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The problem: agents complete 66% of real tasks (humans 72%), yet only 5% of companies have every critical control, and the average organisation logs 54 agent incidents a year.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:31.000
What the Gate checks: an agent-specific attack pack mapped to OWASP ASI01–ASI10; an evaluation harness seeded from your real failures; a cost-per-task baseline; a permission audit; an Agent Bill of Materials; the eight-area readiness scorecard.

4
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:44.000
The deliverable: one Evidence Report written for engineering, the CISO and audit — generated inside your estate, with pass rates, mapped findings, cost per task and the BOM, regenerated on every release.

5
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:54.000
How it installs and runs: day 1 a CLI and a container in your own cloud account; connect the agent's configuration, traces and a traffic sample; the first report inside ten working days; the CI gate on every release after.

6
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Published licence prices: Team $6,000 a year for up to three agents (founding licence $3,600 for the first ten customers, locked for two years); Business $18,000 a year; Enterprise $45,000 a year.

7
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Founding licences are open now; early access ships on 20 November 2026, refunded in full if late. Book a 30-minute call at rainkernel.com or write to hello@rainkernel.com.
